From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:11:56 +0000
Subject: Do not leak rpath and build LDFLAGS into adolc.pc

The pkg-config file added -Wl,-rpath,${libdir} and the LDFLAGS used to
build ADOL-C itself to the link line of every program using it.  Drop
both, and move the libraries ADOL-C itself links against (ColPack) to
Libs.private, since they are only needed for static linking.

Forwarded: not-needed (upstream has replaced autotools with CMake)
---
 adolclib.pc.in | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/adolclib.pc.in b/adolclib.pc.in
index fe3341b..42ef161 100644
--- a/adolclib.pc.in
+++ b/adolclib.pc.in
@@ -7,5 +7,6 @@ Name: @adolclib@
 Version: @PACKAGE_VERSION@
 Description: Algorithmic Differentiation Library for C/C++
 Requires: 
-Libs: -L${libdir} -l@adolclib@ -Wl,-rpath,${libdir} @LDFLAGS@ @LIBS@
+Libs: -L${libdir} -l@adolclib@
+Libs.private: @LIBS@
 Cflags: -I${includedir}
